@startuml tool-call-sequence
title RetroAgent - One turn with a tool call

actor User
participant "CLI" as CLI
participant "Turn loop" as Turn
participant "Context builder" as Context
participant "Provider adapter" as Provider
participant "Model" as Model
participant "Permissions" as Permissions
participant "MCP client" as Client
participant "MCP server" as Server
participant "Data layer" as Data
database "Project memory" as DB

User -> CLI : message or model command
CLI -> Turn : start turn

loop until the model answers without tool calls
  Turn -> Context : build system context, tools and state message
  Context -> Data : read state digest
  Data -> DB : query
  Context --> Turn : context within budget
  Turn -> Provider : complete(messages, tools)
  Provider -> Model : request
  Model --> Provider : text and tool calls
  Provider --> Turn : response and token usage
  Turn -> Turn : truncation guard, calibration

  loop for each tool call, in order
    Turn -> Data : record tool call
    Turn -> Permissions : check mode, permission, approval
    alt refused
      Permissions --> Turn : denied
      Turn -> Data : record outcome denied
    else same call repeated, nothing recorded since
      Turn -> Data : record outcome invalid_argument, not dispatched
    else allowed
      opt permission is ask
        Permissions -> User : prompt with code or commands
        User --> Permissions : allow or deny
      end
      Turn -> Client : call tool
      Client -> Server : tools/call
      Server -> Data : read and write records
      Data -> DB : transaction with invariants
      Server --> Client : result or error
      Client --> Turn : result
      Turn -> Data : record outcome
    end
  end
  note over Turn : three model calls in a row with only\nblocked calls stop the turn
end

Turn --> CLI : final answer
CLI --> User : answer and tables
@enduml
